        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions, Cu(NO3)2·3H2O (0.2 g, 1 mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (20 mL), then triethanolamine (0.13 mL, 1 mmol), pivalic acid (0.05 g, 0.5 mmol) and triethylamine (0.5 mL, 3.5 mmol) were added to give a green-blue solution. Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.45 g, 1 mmol) was added to give a deep blue solution, which was stirred for 4 h, allowed to stand, and layered with diethyl ether. Blue crystals of 1 formed after 3–5 d.",
